Package: rltoolsR
Type: Package
Title: Reinforcement Learning Toolkit with 'ggmlR' Backend
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yuri", "Baramykov", email = "lbsbmsu@mail.ru", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-7627-4217")),
    person("Jonas", "Eschmann", role = "cph",
           comment = "Author of the 'RLtools' library included in inst/include/"))
Description: Provides a reinforcement learning toolkit for R with a unified
    environment interface and Gymnasium-style action and observation
    spaces. Environments include continuous control tasks from the
    header-only 'RLtools' C++ library (Eschmann et al., 2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2306.03530> and a batched tic-tac-toe environment.
    Implements proximal policy optimization (PPO) for discrete and
    continuous actions within a generic training loop that accepts
    user-defined algorithms. Neural networks are trained
    with 'ggmlR', with 'Vulkan' GPU acceleration and a transparent CPU
    fallback.
